{"chunk_id": "496c25babcc6", "text": "Sanjaya recounts how the frightened king Jayadratha, after hearing of Arjuna\u2019s vow to kill him for Abhimanyu\u2019s death, seeks reassurance from Drona. Drona admits that although Jayadratha and Arjuna received equal training, Arjuna surpasses him through discipline and yogic practice, yet he promises protection and reminds him that a warrior\u2019s death leads to heavenly reward. Encouraged, Jayadratha resolves to fight. Later Krishna rebukes Arjuna for rashly vowing Jayadratha\u2019s death without consultation, warning of the danger. Meanwhile the Kauravas, terrified by the vow, plan elaborate defenses: Drona will arrange a complex battle formation, and six great warriors will guard Jayadratha so that Arjuna must defeat them first. The passage builds tension for the coming battle and underscores Arjuna\u2019s formidable reputation.\nJayadratha fears Arjuna\u2019s vow of vengeance for Abhimanyu; Drona reassures him and plans a complex battle formation to protect him from Arjuna.\nThemes: fear of Arjuna, war strategy, kshatriya duty and fate, vengeance for Abhimanyu, loyalty to teachers", "vector": [-0.0013086107792332768, -0.008685543201863766, -0.004993361420929432, 0.01119543332606554, 0.002088823588564992, 0.021598270162940025, -0.014240327291190624, 0.0008858923683874309, -0.009894253686070442, -0.009101656265556812, 0.013870448805391788, 0.006753587629646063, 0.002359627513214946, 0.0009643264347687364, 0.0012797140516340733, 0.018943069502711296, 0.05157164856791496, -0.008163750171661377, 0.015680212527513504, -0.02394964173436165, -0.0030548011418431997, -0.005739723797887564, 0.0023348587565124035, 0.029431771486997604, 0.0021796419750899076, 0.02585187368094921, -0.014174277894198895, -0.02614249289035797, 0.012899517081677914, -0.007774056401103735, -0.0010675291996449232, -0.0021119408775120974, 0.002174688270315528, 0.0049636391922831535, -0.03479501232504845, 0.007384362630546093, 0.0003531597903929651, -0.02